  "reason": "The current best (config_031, acc=0.6776) uses scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder. The largest single improvement in the search came from upgrading the RNA encoder (pca_n2000→scvi_n200, +0.039), and RNA is clearly the dominant signal modality (rna_only multiprofile=0.591 vs image_only=0.208). config_043 isolates the RNA encoder change to scgpt while holding all other settings at their proven-best values (multimodal, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted). This tests whether a more sophisticated, biologically-informed encoder (scgpt) can further improve the RNA representation beyond scvi_n200. It is the highest-expected-value single-variable experiment given that the RNA modality drives most of the signal and encoder quality has been the strongest lever so far. If it improves, we lock in a new best for the final experiment; if not, the remaining experiment can test the image encoder upgrade (config_037)."
